        <div style="border-right: 1px solid var(--line-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); padding: 24px"><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">0</p><p style="margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px">false positives in MoatBench on 0.12.0 (2026-10-30), every scenario run as nine agents' hook payloads</p></div>
        <div style="border-right: 1px solid var(--line-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); padding: 24px"><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">3 OS</p><p style="margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px">macOS, Linux and Windows in CI for every pull request</p></div>
        <div style="border-right: 1px solid var(--line-2); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line-2); padding: 24px"><p style="margin: 0; font-size: 40px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.02em">No model</p><p style="margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px">written rules decide, so the same call gets the same answer every time</p></div>
